["--help"]:
NAME
    hanzo - manage Hanzo AI cloud resources and developer workflow

SYNOPSIS
    hanzo GROUP | COMMAND [FLAGS] [--config=FILE] [--verbose] [--help]
    hanzo [FLAGS] [TASK] [-- PASSTHROUGH...]

DESCRIPTION
    The hanzo CLI manages authentication, billing, and every product of the
    Hanzo AI cloud. Each GROUP below is one product; its subcommands are the
    product's operations, generated from the same contract the API, SDKs and
    MCP tools serve.

    `hanzo` on its own starts an AI coding session, and `hanzo "fix the
    failing test"` starts one on that task (`hanzo dev` is the same). Sign
    in with `hanzo auth login`; see your money with `hanzo billing balance`
    and `hanzo usage`.

    `hanzo console` (or `hanzo dashboard`) launches the interactive fleet
    operations console over agent sandboxes, compute nodes, and local model mesh.
    `hanzo sandbox` (or `sbx`) manages isolated agent workspaces and environments.
    `hanzo monitor` (or `hanzo top`) inspects real-time cluster GPU inference
    telemetry, token throughput, KV cache usage, and speculative MTP heads.
    `hanzo status` shows cloud health and local inference cluster status.

    `hanzo --cloud "task"` runs in a cloud sandbox; `--watch` follows it.
    `hanzo --cloud` lists runs; `--cloud --resume ID --watch` follows one.
    `hanzo --teleport ID` fetches its branch into a clean checkout.
    `--metered` selects Hanzo models for a local session.

GLOBAL FLAGS
     --config=FILE
        Use a custom CLI config file for this invocation.

     --as=ORG
        Act as this org, as your identity in it when you hold one.

     --verbose, -v
        Increase logging verbosity (repeat for more).

     --help
        Display this page, or a subcommand's detailed help.

GROUPS
    GROUP is one of the following:

     3d
       `3d` cloud operations.

     account
       Your own account: API keys you mint and revoke, and org onboarding.

     ad
       Your paid ad campaigns, launched and paused from one place.

     affiliate
       A partner program that pays commission on what your referrals spend.

     agent
       Autonomous agents for your org: define them, run them, keep every run.

     ai
       Hanzo AI — the model API on /v1 (/v1/chat/completions, /v1/messages,
       /v1/models and the rest of…

     allowance
       How much a plan lets you do without paying, and how much of it you
       have left in the window that…

     analytics
       Implements the canonical /v1/analytics/* API, metric catalog,
       automatic query planner, IAM tenant…

     ask
       A plain-language question about your business, answered with real
       numbers.

     audio
       `audio` cloud operations.

     audit
       Your org's tamper-evident audit trail: every security-relevant event,
       hash-chained and readable.

     auth
       Manage identities and credentials.

     author
       A royalty for open-source work: your repo runs, you get paid.

     authz
       The access decision behind an org-scoped call: who may do what, where,
       answered allow or deny.

     auto
       Workflows that run themselves, on a schedule or a webhook.

     base
       Managed Hanzo Base: a hosted backend for your app — collections,
       records, access rules and sign-in.

     benchmark
       One honest score for any model, on the tests everyone quotes.

     billing
       Your org's balance, what it has spent, and the cards it pays with.

     blueprint
       What a template costs to run, worked out before you deploy.

     bot
       Run a local Hanzo Bot gateway or embedded agent wired to local LLMs,
