COMMANDS
    COMMAND is one of the following:

     beat
       Keep this machine present in the fleet: one beat every 30s, no shell,
       no session. Run it under a service manager so the console and the
       scheduler see the box between sessions instead of an hour after the
       last one.

     build
       Build a container image with BuildKit, inside a hanzo-vm microVM.

     code
       Search, index and read code through the cloud's code index.

     connect
       Connect a social or messaging channel via OAuth
       (`/v1/channel/connect`).

     console
       Open the interactive fleet operations console (sandboxes, compute
       nodes, GPU mesh).

     desktop
       Point an agent at the desktop and browser instead of the repo.

     dev
       Start a coding session: a coding agent with the Hanzo MCP toolset
       attached, on the account its tool is signed in to (`--metered` for
       Hanzo's metered models), and the session streamed live to mission
       control. Use `--cloud` to execute the task remotely in a Hanzo
       sandbox.

     doctor
       Check installed tools, paths, authentication, GPU runtime and release
       integrity.

     down
       Stop the local k3s microVM started by `hanzo up`.

     help
       Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s).

     init
       Initialize a new Hanzo project.

     k8s
       Manage the Hanzo Kubernetes cluster over Zero-Trust (`k8s.hanzo` on
       :26443) or pass kubectl args through.

     load
       Pull and load models across the distributed cluster fleet (DGX Spark &
       Strix Halo).

     login
       Sign in through Hanzo IAM (OIDC) — `hanzo auth login` at the top
       level.

     ls
       List active sandboxes, runc containers, & agent workspaces.

     monitor
       Live telemetry inspector and cluster dashboard for GPU inference
       cluster & models.

     pull
       Pull local AI model weights into the shared Hugging Face cache (`hanzo
       engine pull <model>`).

     report
       Collect and share a redacted coding session & diagnostic report with
       Hanzo.

     scan
       Scan local files for exposed secrets (exits non-zero on a find).

     share
       Publish a local service to a public https://<token>.share.hanzo.ai URL.

     status
       Show the whole cloud: what is unhealthy first, then clusters,
       applications and the machines on the fleet.

     upgrade
       Upgrade every Hanzo tool (hanzo, mcp, gen, zt) to its current release,
       and every coding agent installed: npm agents under ~/.hanzo, the rest
       by their own updater (`claude update`, `goose update`, …) or uv.
       Name a tool to upgrade only it; naming an npm agent (gemini, qwen,
       opencode, …) installs it.

     version
       Print the CLI version.

     vm
       Run the hanzo-vm microVM CLI, args passed through verbatim.

     whoami
       Show who you are signed in as and in which org — `hanzo auth show`
       at the top level.


